// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded tan(pi x) of F16
//
// x splits into x1 + x2: x1 keeps the top 11 bits of the F16 encoding, x2 the sign, the exponent and the low 5
// mantissa bits. Then tan(pi x) = sin(pi (x1 + x2)) / cos(pi (x1 + x2)), both expanded by the addition formulas over
// F32 tables of sin and cos of pi x1 and pi x2, tuned so that the F32 quotient rounds correctly to F16 (all but
// sin(pi x1) are sin_pi's tables). Integers and half-integers are settled from the encoding. Round to nearest only.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/tanpi/tanpif16.c via RazorForge's B16Tanpi.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

